{
  "title": { "en": "Mend across the diagonal" },
  "tray": "pipeline",
  "after": {
    "en": "The erased patch looks most like its far-off twin, so in one step it fetched the missing pixels from the opposite corner. That is self-attention: each patch (token) scores every patch with q·k/√d, softmax turns the scores into weights that sum to 1, and the v are averaged with those weights. Stack L layers of 3×3 convolution and you still only see (2L+1)×(2L+1)."
  },
  "intro": [
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "The <part-ref to=\"attention\"></part-ref> in the tray cuts the 16×16 image into 16 patches of 4×4, and every patch asks every patch. The \"q scale\" parameter scales up all the scores: the larger it is, the more each patch looks only at the few most alike."
      }
    },
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "In each test image, two opposite corners hold the same small pattern, but one has had a few pixels erased; one set has nothing erased. This level allows at most 3 nodes. The question is: where else in the image does an erased pixel still show what it looked like?"
      },
      "fig": {
        "test": 0,
        "caption": { "en": "Set 1: the top-left pattern is missing a few pixels" }
      }
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "5-2",
      "kind": "graph",
      "brief": {
        "en": "Two opposite corners hold the same pattern, but a few pixels of one copy have been erased. Restore them and leave everything else unchanged; at most 3 nodes."
      },
      "hint": {
        "en": "A 3×3 part only sees one pixel away at a time. Attention lets each patch compare itself with every patch; the larger the q scale, the more it looks only at the few most similar ones."
      },
      "constraint": { "nodes": { "max": 3 } },
      "scene": "mend",
      "tests": [
        {
          "label": { "en": "Top left erased" },
          "items": [
            { "tile": "X", "at": [0, 0], "erased": [[0, 0], [1, 1], [3, 3]] },
            { "tile": "X", "at": [3, 3] },
            { "tile": "C", "at": [0, 3] },
            { "tile": "P", "at": [2, 1] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": { "en": "Bottom right erased" },
          "items": [
            { "tile": "R", "at": [0, 0] },
            { "tile": "R", "at": [3, 3], "erased": [[1, 0], [0, 1], [3, 2]] },
            { "tile": "K", "at": [1, 2] },
            { "tile": "S", "at": [3, 0] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": { "en": "Top right erased" },
          "items": [
            { "tile": "S", "at": [0, 3], "erased": [[0, 3], [1, 3], [2, 2]] },
            { "tile": "S", "at": [3, 0] },
            { "tile": "X", "at": [1, 1] },
            { "tile": "R", "at": [2, 3] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": { "en": "Both pairs erased" },
          "items": [
            { "tile": "C", "at": [0, 0], "erased": [[0, 0], [3, 0]] },
            { "tile": "C", "at": [3, 3] },
            { "tile": "K", "at": [0, 3] },
            { "tile": "K", "at": [3, 0], "erased": [[0, 1], [3, 3], [2, 2]] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": { "en": "Nothing erased" },
          "items": [
            { "tile": "P", "at": [0, 0] },
            { "tile": "P", "at": [3, 3] },
            { "tile": "R", "at": [1, 2] },
            { "tile": "C", "at": [2, 0] }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "hidden": [
        {
          "label": { "en": "Bottom left erased" },
          "items": [
            { "tile": "K", "at": [3, 0], "erased": [[0, 0], [1, 1], [2, 2]] },
            { "tile": "K", "at": [0, 3] },
            { "tile": "R", "at": [1, 1] },
            { "tile": "C", "at": [2, 2] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": { "en": "All four corners filled" },
          "items": [
            { "tile": "P", "at": [0, 3], "erased": [[1, 1], [1, 3]] },
            { "tile": "P", "at": [3, 0] },
            { "tile": "X", "at": [0, 0] },
            { "tile": "S", "at": [3, 3] },
            { "tile": "C", "at": [1, 2] }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "solution": ["a = attention[s=8](in)", "t = threshold[t=0.3](a)", "out <- t"],
      "naive": ["b = box3(in)", "c = box3(b)", "t = threshold[t=0.2](c)", "out <- t"],
      "alsoFails": [
        ["a = attention(in)", "t = threshold[t=0.3](a)", "out <- t"],
        ["a = attention[s=8](in)", "t = threshold(a)", "out <- t"],
        ["t = threshold(in)", "out <- t"]
      ]
    }
  ]
}
